      "rationale": "The dotplot approximates the sampling distribution of the sample mean, so each dot summarizes a whole sample of 50 households. The Central Limit Theorem says this distribution of sample means is approximately normal for a large enough sample size, while individual bills in the population stay right-skewed."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "B",
      "choice_text": "Each dot is one household's bill, and the dotplot should be right-skewed like the population.",
