      "choice_text": "Each dot is one sample's mean bill, and the dotplot should be right-skewed because the samples come from a right-skewed population.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "This assumes the sampling distribution inherits the population's shape. Averaging 50 bills dampens extreme values, and the Central Limit Theorem says the distribution of sample means is approximately normal for a large enough sample size despite a skewed population. Fix: Check whether the graph shows a statistic from many samples; if it shows sample means with large n, apply the Central Limit Theorem."
